# Live Fir Resource Status

Report current availability or queue pressure at the scope requested. Query Fir
through the established connection; use `connect` if needed. Do not run these
commands on a laptop or a different cluster.

Saved user: `{{FIR_USERNAME}}`; account: `{{FIR_ACCOUNT}}`; preferred GPU type:
`{{FIR_GPU_TYPE}}`. These are context, not proof of current eligibility or availability.

## Node availability

```bash
sinfo -p gpubase_bygpu_b1 -N -o '%N %G %C %e %t'
```

Fir repeats physical nodes across its time bands; use one representative band to
avoid double counting. `%G` lists configured GPU resources, not free GPUs. Inspect
allocation details (`scontrol show node <node>`, including GresUsed/AllocTRES) when
needed to estimate free full H100s or MIG slices. Distinguish measured allocation
from an estimate, and do not treat a mixed node as entirely free. Drained or reserved
capacity may not be schedulable even when hardware appears idle.

## Queue context, when relevant

For a whole-GPU queue view, include all GPU bands; the node-view shortcut does not
cover every queued job:

```bash
GPUPARTS=gpubase_bygpu_b1,gpubase_bygpu_b2,gpubase_bygpu_b3,gpubase_bygpu_b4,gpubase_bygpu_b5,gpubase_bynode_b1,gpubase_bynode_b2,gpubase_bynode_b3,gpubase_bynode_b4,gpubase_bynode_b5,gpubase_interac
squeue -p "$GPUPARTS" -t R,PD -o '%i %u %a %T %M %b %R'
```

Summarize by profile, pending reason, or user/account only as needed to answer
the question. Use `slurm-queue` for the user's job overview and `slurm-resource`
for account eligibility. Query `seff <jobid>` only when completed-job efficiency
is relevant; a free-GPU question does not require an efficiency audit.

For sizing advice, use `ccdb-clusters` and the workload's measurements. Fir GPU
requests use `--gpus-per-node=<gpu_type>:<count>`, never `--partition`, `--gres`,
or `--constraint`. A status check does not authorize a smoke test or submission.

Report the observation time, available evidence, important blockers, and a request
recommendation only when workload needs are known. Do not promise a queue start
time or hide failed queries behind an empty report.
